"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[4142],{39943:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"Opens a connection to the named ordered datastore, scheduling a reconnect\\nloop if the initial connect fails.\\n\\nAlso installs the `PlayerRemoving` flush: any write still parked behind the\\n`UPDATE_DELAY` timer for a departing player is cancelled and replayed\\nimmediately, so leaving the server does not drop the player\'s last score.","params":[{"name":"dataStoreName","desc":"name of the ordered datastore to wrap","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"OrderedDB"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":99,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"WipePlayerData","desc":"Permanently removes a user\'s entry from the datastore.\\n\\n`RemoveAsync` is not throttled the way the other request types are, so this\\nskips the request-budget wait entirely.","params":[{"name":"userId","desc":"user whose entry to delete","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"the removed value, or nil on failure","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":147,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"GetTopValues","desc":"Returns the top `count` entries in descending order.\\n\\nPages through `GetSortedAsync` rather than assuming one page holds\\neverything: it re-checks `IsFinished` at each page boundary and waits for\\nrequest budget again before advancing, so a large `count` spanning several\\npages stays within throttle limits. Indexing is offset by page so entries\\nare read in true rank order.\\n\\nA failed `GetSortedAsync` warns, waits a second and retries by recursing.\\n\\nIn Studio without `SaveInStudio`, returns fabricated entries \u2014 the players\\ncurrently in the server first, then random user ids \u2014 so leaderboard UI has\\nsomething to render.","params":[{"name":"count","desc":"how many entries to return","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"ranked entries, key is the stringified UserId","lua_type":"{ { key: string, value: number } }"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":183,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"GetValue","desc":"Reads one user\'s value.\\n\\nChecks the pending `queue` first so a value written this session is visible\\nbefore it has reached the datastore. Returns nil for a user with no entry\\nand `false` when the read itself failed \u2014 distinguish the two if the caller\\ncares about the difference.\\n\\nIn Studio without `SaveInStudio`, returns a random integer.","params":[{"name":"userId","desc":"user to read","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"the value, nil when unset, false on read failure","lua_type":"any"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":310,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"SetValue","desc":"Writes a user\'s value, coalesced behind the `UPDATE_DELAY` timer.\\n\\nBy default the write goes through `UpdateAsync` and keeps whichever of the\\nold and new values is larger \u2014 a leaderboard score only climbs. Pass\\n`forceSet` to use `SetAsync` and overwrite unconditionally, which is what\\n[LeaderboardService] does when flushing a final coin balance that may have\\ngone down.\\n\\nThe value is floored, since ordered datastores reject non-integers. Non-number\\nand nil values warn and no-op. A user who is not in the server implies\\n`skipDelay`.","params":[{"name":"userId","desc":"user to write","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"newValue","desc":"value to store; floored","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"forceSet","desc":"sets the value without checking if it\'s higher","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"name":"skipDelay","desc":"write immediately instead of coalescing","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":367,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"AddToValue","desc":"Adds a delta to a user\'s value, coalesced behind the `UPDATE_DELAY` timer.\\n\\nThe addition happens inside `UpdateAsync`, so it is applied against whatever\\nthe datastore currently holds rather than a value read earlier \u2014 concurrent\\nservers accumulate correctly.\\n\\n:::caution Coalescing discards, it does not accumulate\\nA second `AddToValue` for the same user within the delay window **cancels**\\nthe pending one and replaces its value rather than summing the two deltas.\\nCallers that add repeatedly should accumulate their own total and write it\\nonce, or pass `skipDelay`.\\n:::\\n\\nThe delta is floored. Non-number and nil values warn and return false.","params":[{"name":"userId","desc":"user to write","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"valueToAdd","desc":"delta to add; floored","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"skipDelay","desc":"write immediately instead of coalescing","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"false on a bad value or while disconnected","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":502,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"UpdateValue","desc":"Runs an arbitrary transform against a user\'s stored value via `UpdateAsync`.\\n\\nThe escape hatch for logic the max-keeping [OrderedDB:SetValue] and the\\nadditive [OrderedDB:AddToValue] cannot express. Unlike those two this is\\n**not** coalesced \u2014 it writes immediately, after waiting for request budget.","params":[{"name":"userId","desc":"user to update","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"updateCallback","desc":"receives the stored value, returns the new one","lua_type":"(oldValue: number?) -> number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the update succeeded","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":612,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"_tryReconnect","desc":"Retries the datastore connection every 5 seconds until it succeeds,\\nre-scheduling itself on each failure.\\n\\nReturns immediately rather than yielding \u2014 the retry runs on a delayed\\nthread and assigns `_connectedDataStore` when it lands, so the return value\\nis always nil.","params":[{"name":"dataStoreName","desc":"datastore to reconnect to","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"always nil; the connection lands asynchronously","lua_type":"OrderedDataStore?"}],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":658,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}},{"name":"_connect","desc":"Attempts one connection to the ordered datastore, warning and returning nil\\non failure rather than propagating the error.","params":[{"name":"dataStoreName","desc":"datastore to open","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"the store, or nil on failure","lua_type":"OrderedDataStore?"}],"function_type":"method","private":true,"source":{"line":686,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"OrderedDB","desc":"Class that manages a connection to an ordered datastore.\\n\\nAuthor: Zach (InfinityDesign)\\n\\nOne instance wraps one OrderedDataStore, and [LeaderboardService] creates\\none per leaderboard. On top of the raw store it adds four things:\\n\\n**Resilient connection.** `GetOrderedDataStore` is wrapped in a pcall; a\\nfailure schedules [OrderedDB._tryReconnect], which retries every 5 seconds\\nindefinitely. Write methods return false while disconnected rather than\\nerroring, so a datastore outage degrades instead of breaking callers.\\n\\n**Write coalescing.** [OrderedDB:SetValue] and [OrderedDB:AddToValue] do not\\nwrite immediately \u2014 they park the value in `_lastPlayerCalls` behind an\\n`UPDATE_DELAY` (30s) timer. A newer call for the same user cancels the\\npending one, so a player earning points repeatedly costs one write rather\\nthan dozens. The deferred write re-checks that it is still the current\\npending call, both before and after waiting on request budget, and abandons\\nitself if superseded.\\n\\nThe corresponding risk is a lost write when a player leaves mid-delay, so\\n`PlayerRemoving` cancels the timer and immediately replays the pending call\\nwith `skipDelay`. Calls for a user who is not in the server skip the delay\\nentirely.\\n\\n**Budget awareness.** Every datastore call first spins until\\n`GetRequestBudgetForRequestType` reports at least 3 requests available,\\nkeeping the store clear of Roblox\'s throttle.\\n\\n**Monotonic writes.** [OrderedDB:SetValue] writes through `UpdateAsync` and\\nkeeps the larger of the old and new values, so a leaderboard score can only\\nclimb. `forceSet` switches to `SetAsync` for the cases that must overwrite\\ndownward. All values are floored \u2014 ordered datastores reject non-integers.\\n\\n:::info Studio\\nGated on `FeatureFlags.SaveInStudio` (on by default). When it is off and the\\nserver is Studio, reads return random mock data ([OrderedDB:GetTopValues]\\nfabricates a page seeded from the players present) and writes early-return\\ntrue without touching a datastore.\\n:::\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":49,"path":"src/Server/Class/DB/OrderedDB.luau"}}')}}]);